<header><p class="st-kicker">margraviate · Italy</p><h1 class="st-title">March of Friuli</h1><p class="st-meta">776 CE – 952 CE (approx.) · capital Cividale del Friuli</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Carolingian frontier march in north-eastern Italy whose margrave Berengar became King of Italy and emperor.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After Duke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hrodgaud">Hrodgaud's</a> revolt in 776, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charlemagne">Charlemagne</a> replaced the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-lombards">Lombard</a> dukes of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/friuli">Friuli</a> with Frankish officials. The territory was expanded into a march facing the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/avars">Avars</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavs">Slavs</a>, and its margraves commanded forces that, under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eric-of-friuli">Eric of Friuli</a>, captured the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/avar-ring">Avar Ring</a> and its treasure in 796.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The march was a military command reaching from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alps">Alps</a> to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/histria">Istria</a> and into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pannonia">Pannonia</a>, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cividale-del-friuli">Cividale</a> as its centre. After 828 it was reorganised, and from about 846 it was held by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unruochings">Unruoching</a> family, beginning with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eberhard-of-friuli">Eberhard</a>, a cultured noble who married <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-the-pious">Louis the Pious's</a> daughter Gisela and owned a notable library. His son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berengar-i-of-italy">Berengar</a> became margrave in 874.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berengar-i-of-italy">Berengar of Friuli</a> was elected King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> in 888 and crowned emperor in 915, while <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungarian-invasions-of-europe">Hungarian raids</a> devastated the region. In 952 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/otto-i">Otto I</a> took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/friuli">Friuli</a> from Italian control and attached it, with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/commune-of-verona">Verona</a>, to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/duchy-of-bavaria">Duchy of Bavaria</a> as the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/march-of-verona">March of Verona</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/march-of-friuli.jpg" alt="March of Friuli" width="320" height="314"><figcaption>Image: Awarenmark-frankenreich.png: Tsui Das Frankenreich von 771–843Simplificado-es.svg: rowanwindwhistler derivative work:... · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Awarenmark-frankenreich-es.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>776 CE – 952 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>margraviate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Cividale del Friuli</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Eric of Friuli, Eberhard of Friuli, Berengar I</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Latin, Old High German</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Italy, Slovenia</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Margraviate of Friuli</dd></dl></aside></div>
